    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Mauryan Empire was established by Chandragupta Maurya in 322 BCE with guidance from Chanakya after overthrowing the Nanda Dynasty.",
        "Megasthenes, the Greek ambassador sent by Seleucus Nicator, wrote 'Indica', detailing Mauryan society and imperial administration.",
        "Emperor Ashoka embraced Buddhism after witnessing the devastation of the Kalinga War in 261 BCE and promulgated his policy of 'Dhamma'.",
        "Ashokan Edicts were mostly written in Prakrit language using the Brahmi script, which was deciphered by James Prinsep in 1837.",
        "The administration was highly centralized, operating on the 'Saptanga Theory' of statecraft detailed in Kautilya's Arthashastra."
      ],
      "id": "a3g262p"
    },
